      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I understand—when the foundation itself is gone, \"recovery\" can feel like a cruel joke, not a goal. But a blown-up track doesn't erase your ability to walk; it just means you have to find a new path, even if it's over rubble. Reputation is loud, but it's not the same as worth—people forget faster than you think, especially when they see you keep moving. You don't have to rebuild the old life today, but you can choose one defiant action that says \"I'm still here.\"",
